<title>CHILE: Endesa to invest $60 mln in transmission.</title>
<headline>Endesa to invest $60 mln in transmission.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean power utility Empresa Nacional de Electricidad (Endesa) said its Transelec unit would invest $60 million in four new transmission projects during the next two years.</p>
<p>The projects involve expanding and upgrading two transmission lines in southern Chile and building a line to supply power to the Los Pelambres copper mine, which is about to start a major expansion plan.</p>
<p>((--Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
